  "course_code": "COMP385",
  "course_title": "Theory of Computing",
  "course_description": "This course is the study of topics that include the theory of finite state machines and automata; regular expressions; Turing machines; grammars; parsing; the language hierarchy; machine design and construction; computability; insolvability; and the halting problem. The course also discusses issuses in the equivalence of various computational models and characterizations. Prerequisites: COMP 360.(F;S;SS)",
